-- title:
--   Graph element $p\in\mathrm{Her}(a)$ with full signal where $\|\pi(a)\|>1/2$ and a defect that can vanish only where $\|\pi(y)\|\le1/4$
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a unital C*-algebra, ordered by its cone of positive elements. For $h\in A$ let $\mathrm{Her}(h)=\overline{\{hah^*: a\in A\}}$ (for $h\ge0$ the hereditary C*-subalgebra generated by $h$). An element $z\in A$ is *properly infinite* if $\operatorname{diag}(z,z)$ is Cuntz-below $z$: there is a sequence of $1\times2$ matrices $r_j$ over $A$ with $r_j^*\,z\,r_j\to\operatorname{diag}(z,z)$ in $M_2(A)$. A *representation* of $A$ is a unital $*$-homomorphism $\pi\colon A\to B(H)$ into the bounded operators on a complex Hilbert space $H$.
--
--   Let $a,y,c\in A$ with $a\ge0$, $y\ge0$ and $\|c\|\le1$, and assume that every positive element of $\mathrm{Her}(a)$ is properly infinite. Then there is $p\in\mathrm{Her}(a)$ with $p\ge0$ and $\|p\|\le1$ such that for every representation $\pi$ of $A$:
--
--   1. if $\|\pi(a)\|>\tfrac12$, then $\|\pi(p)\|=1$;
--   2. if $\pi\big(y(1-c^*p^2c)y\big)=0$, then $\|\pi(y)\|\le\tfrac14$.
--
--   In display form:
--   $$
--   \|\pi(a)\|>\tfrac12\ \Longrightarrow\ \|\pi(p)\|=1,\qquad\qquad \pi\big(y(1-c^*p^2c)y\big)=0\ \Longrightarrow\ \|\pi(y)\|\le\tfrac14 .
--   $$
--
--   The element $p$ is a signal for $a$: it is fully visible in every representation in which $a$ is large. At the same time, $c^*p^2c$ cannot act as the identity on $y$ (the defect $y(1-c^*p^2c)y$ cannot vanish) in any representation in which $y$ is not small. This qualitative nonvanishing statement starts the local shrinking step. The quantitative nonvanishing theorem then upgrades it to a uniform lower bound on the defect.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The order on $A$ is `CStarAlgebra.spectralOrder`; proper infiniteness is `OAI.MainGap.ProperlyInfinite`. Representations are `HilbertRep.{u,v} A` (Hilbert spaces in a fixed universe `v`), and $p$ is chosen before, and independently of, the representation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/CStarAlgebra/PureInfiniteness/Graph.lean#L590-L634

